{
  "presses": ["L-pinky-top", "L-ring-home", "L-middle-bottom", "R-index-home-in"],
  "note": "T1 pressed: {L-pinky-top, L-ring-home, L-middle-bottom, R-index-home-in}. Record returned sorted symbols next turn; update possible-letter sets for those 4. No locks yet. Plan: keep overlapping chords to isolate each key despite rotations; note rotated keys each turn."
}

{
  "presses": ["R-index-home-in", "R-index-top", "R-ring-top", "L-ring-home"],
  "locks": {
    "R-ring-top": "V"
  },
  "note": "T4: set {I,O,P,V} with L-ring-home=I (not rotated into T4). Constraints imply R-index-home-in∈{O,P} and R-index-top∉{V}; hence R-ring-top=V (not in T4 rotation notice). Thus (R-index-home-in,R-index-top) are {O,P} in unknown order. L-ring-home rotated after T4 so not fixed now. Plan T5 chord {R-ring-top(V), R-index-home-in, R-index-top, L-ring-home} to resolve O/P via symbol multiset."
}

{
  "presses": [
    "R-index-home-in",
    "R-ring-top",
    "L-ring-home",
    "L-pinky-home"
  ],
  "locks": {
    "R-ring-top": "V"
  },
  "note": "T5 chord gave {O,P,S,V}; using T4 constraints => R-ring-top=V fixed (not rotated in T4/T5). Also R-index-home-in∈{O,P} (R-index-top had the other). T6 press {R-index-home-in, R-ring-top(V), L-ring-home, L-pinky-home} to see whether L-pinky-home is O/P; if only one of {O,P} appears, that letter is R-index-home-in."
}

{
  "presses": ["L-ring-bottom", "R-index-home-in", "R-index-top-in", "R-middle-top"],
  "locks": {
    "L-ring-bottom": "S",
    "R-index-home-in": "O"
  },
  "note": "From T8 set {F,O,S,V}: deduce L-ring-bottom=S (since T7 swap L-ring-home↔L-ring-bottom and S in list), and R-index-home-in=O (since R-index-home-in∈{O,P} and P not in list). Remaining {F,V} are {R-ring-top,L-ring-home} (unknown). Also T8 rotation swapped R-index-top-in↔R-middle-top; T9 presses include those two + known S/O to resolve them."
}

{
  "presses": ["L-ring-home", "L-ring-bottom", "R-index-home-in", "R-middle-home"],
  "note": "T10 no rotation. Chord {R-index-top-in,L-ring-bottom,R-index-home-in,L-ring-home}->{F,O,Q,S} => L-ring-home=F, L-ring-bottom=S, R-index-home-in=O, R-index-top-in=Q. From T9 set {R-index-top-in,R-middle-top}={K,Q} => R-middle-top=K (T9 rotation only L-pinky-top & R-index-bottom, so K stable). Plan T11: press {L-ring-home(F),L-ring-bottom(S),R-index-home-in(O),R-middle-home} to learn R-middle-home."
}

{
  "presses": ["L-pinky-top", "L-ring-home", "R-ring-home", "R-middle-home"],
  "note": "Update: R-index-bottom-in=E. Still unresolved: L-pinky-top vs L-index-home = {H,M}. (Known: L-ring-home=F, L-middle-top=C, L-ring-bottom=S, R-middle-top=K, R-ring-home=B, R-ring-top=V, R-middle-home=I, R-index-home-in=O, R-index-top-in=Q). Next: press L-pinky-top + {L-ring-home(F), R-ring-home(B), R-middle-home(I)} to pin whether L-pinky-top=H or M (use rotation notice)."
}

{
  "presses": ["L-ring-home", "R-ring-home", "R-middle-home", "L-ring-top"],
  "note": "From t18: L-pinky-top=H so L-index-home=M. Known: L-pinky-top H; L-ring-home F; L-ring-bottom S; L-middle-top C; L-index-home M; R-middle-top K; R-ring-home B; R-ring-top V; R-middle-home I; R-index-home-in O; R-index-top-in Q; R-index-bottom-in E. Next (t20): press L-pinky-home + {L-ring-home(F), R-ring-home(B), R-middle-home(I)} to deduce L-pinky-home letter (update if any rotation from t19)."
}
